##

8_29_setting_up_my_website {
    standard_header;
    top_bar("8_29_setting_up_my_website");
    div {
        "background-color" : pebble_color_D2;
        "min-height" : "300vh";
        "display" : "flex";
        "align-items" : "center";
        "flex-direction" : "column";

        text "Setting up my website" {
            "color" : golden_color_L1;
            "font-size" : "2rem";
            "font-weight" : "900";
            "margin" : "16 0 16 0px";
            main_font;
        }

    div {
        "background-color" : pebble_color_D1;
        "border-radius" : "8px";
        "width" : "100%";
        "max-width" : "700px";
        "padding" : "8px";
        "display" : "flex";
        "flex-direction" : "column";

        collapse_section("What is this website ^",capture_node(section_getting_started),"","");
        div section_getting_started {
            "height" : "0px";
            "overflow-y" : "hidden";
            "transition" : "height 0.6s ease";  
            text "This website is a place for me to put my blog posts, contact details, and documentation for my projects." {post_text_theme;} 
            text "Intially I had just a GitHub page, and I did one blog post with some essays about 6 months ago, but it made me realize my work wasn't ready to be public yet." {post_text_theme;}
            text "Now that I'm close to shipping my first project for a client, I'm comfortable finally revealing myself to the world, and thus: this website." {post_text_theme;}
        }

        collapse_section("Technical asides ^",capture_node(section_technical_asides),"","");
        div section_technical_asides {
            "height" : "0px";
            "overflow-y" : "hidden";
            "transition" : "height 0.6s ease";  
            text "I have a technical aside I want to go off on, yet most readers of this post probably aren't here to listen to me talk about language design. So ironically, the first element of this blog post is probably going to be adding the mechanism to make the technical aside collapsable." {post_text_theme;} 
            text "To do this, I'll just use some JavaScript, given as it's a client side presentation concern. I'll basically just steal the code I use in the top bar on smaller screens. I don't want to use the exact arrow design, because I want more of an expand down and to the side, so that the label of 'technical aside' remains there." {post_text_theme;}
        }


        collapse_section("Aside: route registration is too verbose ^",capture_node(Aside_route_registration_is_too_verbose),"","");
        div Aside_route_registration_is_too_verbose {
            "height" : "0px";
            "overflow-y" : "hidden";
            "transition" : "height 0.6s ease";  
            "background-color" : pebble_color_D1;

            text "Welcome to the techincal aside! Here's what the code to make this button work looks like:" 
            {
               post_text_theme;
            }

            div {
                "background-color" : "black";
                "margin" : "8px";

                text ""+
                "\n    button {"+
                "\n        \"border\" : \"none\";"+
                "\n        \"background-color\" : pine_color;"+
                "\n        \"border-radius\" : \"12px\";"+
                "\n        \"padding\" : \"0 16 0 16px\";"+
                "\n        text \"Aside: route registration is too verbose ^\" {"+
                "\n                    \"margin\" : \"5px\"; \"font-weight\" : \"700\";"+
                "\n                    \"color\" : golden_color_L1; main_font;"+
                "\n          }"+
                "\n        \"onclick\" : \""+
                "\n            const el = getel(\"+js_lit(capture_node(Aside_route_registration_is_too_verbose))+\");"+
                "\n            if(el.style.height === '0px') {"+
                "\n                el.style.height = el.scrollHeight + 'px';"+
                "\n                this.children[0].innerText = 'Aside: route registration is too verbose v';"+
                "\n            } else {"+
                "\n                el.style.height = '0px';"+
                "\n                this.children[0].innerText = 'Aside: route registration is too verbose ^';"+
                "\n            }"+
                "\n        \";"+
                "\n    }\n"
                {
                    "white-space" : "pre";
                    "font-size" : "0.8rem";
                    "color" : "white";
                    main_font;
                };
            }

            text "And now, the actual aside.
I'm not happy with the way route registration currently works, it's a bit too verbose and flat. The reason why I use precompiling blocks and register a new language keyword is so that I can assign stage based behaviour, since TwigSnap used to use POST and FRAG handlers rather than the modern RUN system.  So when I'm registering the route for this post it looks like:" 
            {
               post_text_theme;
            }

            div {
                "background-color" : "black";
                "margin" : "8px";
                text "
    ##
        register \"8_29_setting_up_my_website\";
        \"8_29_setting_up_my_website\" {
            in htmlemiting {
                subemit(\"body\",false,\"\",\"\");
            }
        }
    ##

    8_29_setting_up_my_website {
        standard_header;
        top_bar(\"8_29_setting_up_my_website\");
        div {

        }
    }
                "
                {
                    "white-space" : "pre";
                    "font-size" : "0.8rem";
                    "color" : "white";
                    main_font;
                };
            }
            text "That feels like too much to me, we're restarting the name of the route 3 times and the in htmlemitting behaviour is always the same. But, I promised myself I'd just write the blog today, not go off on a sidequest." 
            {
                post_text_theme;
            }
        }


        collapse_section("Readability ^",capture_node(section_readability),"getel("+js_lit(capture_node(text_demo))+").style.display = 'block'","getel("+js_lit(capture_node(text_demo))+").style.display = 'none'");

        div text_demo {
            "display" : "none";
            "background-color" : pebble_color;
            "margin-left" : "calc(-50vw + 50%)";
            "margin-right" : "calc(-50vw + 50%)";
            "width" : "100vw";
            text "This is how the text currently looks to me on the page, which I'm not very satisfied with at all! It feels almost exahusting to read, probably because of the line length and bright white color and lack of good breaks between lines. So, let me go and try to fix this." {
                "white-space" : "pre-wrap";
                "color" : "white";
                "margin" : "4 8 4 8px";
                "font-size" : "1rem";
                main_font;
            }
        }   
        
        div section_readability {
            "height" : "0px";
            "overflow-y" : "hidden";
            "transition" : "height 0.6s ease";  
            text "I need to actaully make this text readable. That means making a theme: " 
            {
                post_text_theme;
            }

        div {
            "background-color" : "black";
            "margin" : "8px";
            text '
    inlined post_text_theme {
        "white-space" : "pre-wrap";
        "color" : "white";
        "margin" : "4 8 4 8px";
        "font-size" : "1rem";
        main_font;
    }
            ' 
            {
                "white-space" : "pre-wrap";
                "font-size" : "0.8rem";
                "color" : "white";
                main_font;
            };
        }

        text "This can just be dropped in now on each of these paragraphs. Yes, it's basically just a CSS style sheet, and yes, I do have a style attribute I can use to do normal CSS, I just prefer these themes since they can have code in them and it's more local." {post_text_theme;}

        text "And there we go, much better, ignore the fact that the text before looked like this also (I didn't want the blog before this point to be exhausting to read)." {post_text_theme;}
        text "I moved the body into a card on a darker background, then made the text smaller and an off-white, and added more line spacing. The biggest impact though was fixing a max width for the card, it makes the lines a lot less exhausting in length." {post_text_theme;}

        div {
            "background-color" : "black";
            "margin" : "8px";
            text '
    inlined post_text_theme {
        "white-space" : "pre-wrap";
        "color" : " rgb(238, 238, 238)";
        "margin" : "4 8 4 8px";
        "font-size" : "0.9rem";
        "font-weight" : "400";
        "line-height" : "1.5";
        main_font;
    }
            ' 
            {
                "white-space" : "pre-wrap";
                "font-size" : "0.8rem";
                "color" : "white";
                main_font;
            };
        }
        }

        div {
            "border" : "none";
            "background-color" : pine_color_L1;
            "border-radius" : "12px";
            "margin" : "8px";
            text "A Fragment" {"text-align" : "center"; "margin" : "5px"; "font-weight" : "700"; "font-size" : "0.9rem"; "color" : golden_color; main_font;}
        }

        text "I want to preserve a fragment of the website so future readers can see what I was working with." {post_text_theme;}
        text "This will just be a copy paste of the current website code with external themes and such replaced, so it remains as-is." {post_text_theme;}
        text "Though, since it won't be able to change pages, I'll simulate that with a little URL bar which you should see below, keep scrolling to see how I built the website up from here." {post_text_theme;}

        script "function puppet_goTo(label, route) {
            getel('puppet_url_text').innerText = label; Array.from(getel('8_29_pages').children).forEach(e => {
                if(e.id.startsWith(route)) {
                    console.log('Puppet ',e.id,' starts with ',route);
                    e.style.display = 'flex';
                } else {
                    e.style.display = 'none';
                }
            });
        }";
        div {
            "display" : "flex";
            "justify-content" : "center";
            "overflow" : "hidden";
            "border" : "2px solid black";
            "border-radius" : "8px";
            div {
                "display" : "flex";
                "flex-direction" : "column";
                "justify-content" : "center";
                "width" : "100%";
                div {
                    "flex" : "1";
                    "border-radius" : "10 10 0 0px";
                    "display" : "flex";
                    "align-items" : "center";
                    "justify-content" : "center";
                    "overflow" : "hidden";
                    "background-color" : "white";

                    text "At: " {
                        "color" : "black";
                        "font-size" : "14px";
                        "font-weight" : "700";
                        "background-color" : "rgba(0,0,0,0.25)";
                        "height" : "100%";
                        "display" : "flex";
                        "align-items" : "center";
                        "padding" : "0 16px";
                        main_font;
                    }
                    text "/" {
                        "id" : "puppet_url_text";
                        "flex" : "1";
                        "color" : "black";
                        "border" : "none";
                        "font-size" : "14px";
                        "font-weight" : "600";
                        "padding-left" : "12px";
                        main_font;
                    }
                }



                div {
                    div puppet_main_bar {
                        "display" : "flex";
                        "flex-direction" : "row";
                        "align-items" : "center";
                        "justify-content" : "space-between";
                        "padding" : "16px 32px";
                        "width" : "100%";
                        "background-color" : "rgb(31, 60, 27)";
                        div {
                            "display" : "flex";
                            "flex-direction" : "row";
                            "align-items" : "start";  
                            "gap" : "12px"; 

                            "cursor" : "pointer";
                            "onclick" : "puppet_goTo('/','puppet_root_path')";

                            img {
                                "width" : "80px";
                                "height" : "80px";
                                "object-fit" : "contain";
                                "flex-shrink" : "0";
                                "src" : "web/goldensystems/files/old_icon.png";
                            }

                            div {
                                "display" : "flex";
                                "flex-direction" : "column";
                                text "Golden" {
                                    "id" : "title_text";
                                    "margin-bottom" : "0px";
                                    "font-size" : "2.2rem";
                                    "font-weight" : "700";
                                    "color" : golden_color;
                                    main_font;
                                }
                                text "Systems & Software" {
                                    "font-size" : "1rem";
                                    "color" : golden_color_D1;
                                    "font-weight" : "500";
                                    main_font;
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        div {
                            "display" : "flex";
                            "flex-direction" : "row";
                            "gap" : "24px";
                            "align-items" : "center";
                            "overflow-y" : "hidden";
                            "transition" : "height 0.6s ease";

                            stateless template div nav_link(string label, string route) {
                                text label {
                                    "font-size" : "1rem";
                                    "font-weight" : "500";
                                    "color" : golden_color_D1;
                                    "cursor" : "pointer";
                                    "onclick" : "const route = "+js_lit(route)+"; puppet_goTo( '/'+route.split('_').slice(1).join('_'),route)";
                                    main_font;
                                }
                            }

                            nav_link("blog","puppet_blog");
                            nav_link("GDSL","puppet_GDSL_start");
                            nav_link("about","puppet_about");
                            nav_link("contact","puppet_contact");
                        }

                        button {
                            "display" : "none";
                            "border" : "none";
                            "background-color" : pebble_color;
                            "border-radius" : "12px";
                            "width" : "20%";
                            text "v" {"margin" : "5px"; "color" : golden_color_L1; main_font;}
                            "onclick" : "
                                const nav = this.parentElement.children[1];
                                if(nav.style.height === '0px') {
                                    nav.style.height = nav.scrollHeight + 'px';
                                    this.children[0].innerText = '^';
                                } else {
                                    nav.style.height = '0px';
                                    this.children[0].innerText = 'v';
                                }
                            ";
                        }
                    }
                    script "
                        function update_puppet_nav() {
                            const bar = getel("+js_lit(capture_node(puppet_main_bar))+");
                            if(window.innerWidth <= 980) {
                                bar.style.flexDirection = 'column';
                                bar.children[1].style.flexDirection = 'column';
                                bar.children[1].style.height = '0px';
                                bar.children[2].style.display = 'block';
                            } else {
                                bar.style.flexDirection = 'row';
                                bar.children[1].style.flexDirection = 'row';
                                bar.children[1].style.height = 'auto';
                                bar.children[2].style.display = 'none';
                            }
                        }
                        window.addEventListener('resize', update_puppet_nav);
                        update_puppet_nav();
                    ";
                }

                div {
                    "id" : "8_29_pages";
                    div puppet_root_path {
                        "display" : "flex";
                        "flex-direction" : "column";
                        "align-items" : "center";
                        "min-height" : "50vh";
